[32m+[m[32m## Time format[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m`ngx-gantt` uniformly uses the 10-digit UnixTime format. The user needs to ensure that the date value passed in is UnixTime[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## GanttDate[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m`ngx-gantt` provides the `GanttDate` class to handle time. The example is as follows:[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```javascript[m
[32m+[m[32mimport { GanttDate } from 'ngx-gantt';[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mnew GanttDate(new Date('2022-01-01 12:00:00')).getUnixTime(); //[m
[32m+[m[32mnew GanttDate(1617275597).addDays(1);[m
[32m+[m[32mnew GanttDate(1617275597).addHours(24).getDay();[m
[32m+[m[32mnew GanttDate(1617275597).format("yyyy年MM月");[m
[32m+[m[32m...[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32mFor more information, please refer to [GanttDate](https://github.com/worktile/ngx-gantt/blob/master/packages/gantt/src/utils/date.ts)[m
